#: Stocks whose stored spectral density CRITERION is a family inference rather
#: than a reading of their own sheet, with the anchor that licenses it.
#:
#: ⚠ OWNER DECISION 2026-08-26: KEEP THE VALUE, ANNOTATE IT. The note below is
#: appended to each profile's provenance so the inference travels with the data
#: instead of living only in a document.
#:
#: ⚠ AND THE RECORD THIS REPLACES WAS WRONG. From 2026-08-25 to 2026-08-26 this
#: project asserted that NO sheet in the corpus printed a 0.2 criterion, and
#: concluded the value "appears nowhere" and "was supplied for precisely the
#: cases with no evidence for it". A full-corpus sweep found THREE FILES that
#: print it -- `5205t.pdf` p4, `KODAK VISION2 250D ... 5205.pdf` p4 and
#: `5218-Vision2-500T-H-1-5218t.pdf` p4, each carrying "D=0.2>D-min" in the
#: spectral panel's own caption block. The earlier sweep had searched only
#: INSIDE the plot frame, because that is where 5222 and 7239 put the caption;
#: the VISION2 layout puts it BELOW the frame. "Not printed" was really "not
#: printed where I looked" -- the same lesson as the F-125 outlined-vector-art
#: case, reached from the opposite direction.
_CRITERION_FAMILY_INFERENCE: dict[str, str] = {
    n: ("⚠ SPECTRAL CRITERION IS A FAMILY INFERENCE, ANNOTATED 2026-08-26 (owner "
        "decision: keep the value, annotate it). This stock's own sheet prints "
        "only 'Sensitivity = reciprocal of exposure (erg/cm2) required to produce "
        "specified density' and never names the density. The stored "
        "'D0.2_above_dmin' is licensed by a DOCUMENTED ANCHOR INSIDE THE SAME "
        "FAMILY: KODAK VISION2 250D 5205 (both editions on file, p4) and KODAK "
        "VISION2 500T 5218 (p4) print 'D=0.2>D-min' in their spectral panel's own "
        "caption block, directly beneath 'Densitometry: Status M' and beside "
        "'Effective exposure' and 'Process: ECN-2'. Same product line, same H-1 "
        "sheet series, same era. So the 0.2 is a REAL PRINTED KODAK CONVENTION "
        "and not an invention -- what is inferred is only that it carries from "
        "the two sheets that state it to this one, which does not. ⚠ NINE STILL "
        "FILMS in this database also store 0.2 (EKTAR 100, GOLD 100/200, PORTRA "
        "100T/160/400/800, ULTRAMAX 400/800); those are a different product line "
        "in different publications and nothing in this corpus supports or refutes "
        "the value for them. That is the live gap, not this one.")
    for n in ("KODAK_VISION2_200T_5217", "KODAK_VISION3_50D_5203",
              "KODAK_VISION3_250D_5207", "KODAK_VISION3_200T_5213",
              "KODAK_VISION3_500T_5219")
}


