#: DEVELOPMENT PROGRESS TYPE BY DEVELOPING-AGENT CLASS (schema v18,
#: 2026-08-27). Assigned ONLY where the profile's `ProcessingSpec` names the
#: developing agents and they match, by CHEMISTRY, one of the two developers
#: Tani identifies. Nine stocks qualify out of the thirteen that name a
#: developer at all.
#:
#: ⚠ NOT INFERRED FROM PROCESS FAMILY, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. It would be
#: easy to write "every C-41 stock is type A, every B&W negative type B" and
#: cover 150 profiles. Two worked examples are not a survey of developers, and
#: this project's own method rule forbids deriving a class estimate from
#: insufficient sampling. So the four developers whose agent pair does NOT
#: match either example stay UNKNOWN:
#:   * SPD / Super Prodol -- phenidone-hydroquinone (PQ). Tani's type-B example
#:     is metol-hydroquinone (MQ) specifically, and PQ is superadditive through
#:     a different mechanism. Not assumed to behave the same.
#:   * KODAK HC-110, Technidol LC -- agent pair not named in the record.
#:   * "Process E-6" -- names a process, not an agent; E-6 runs a B&W first
#:     developer AND a colour developer, so one enum cannot describe it.
#:
#: THE TWO MATCHES, by chemistry rather than by trade name:
#:   GRANULAR  metol-hydroquinone, the same agent pair as Tani's D72 ->
#:             ILFORD ID-11 and KODAK D-96.
#:   PARALLEL  4-amino-N-dialkylaniline, the same agent class as Tani's CP-20
#:             -> Soviet ЦПВ-1, whose own recorded formula names
#:             "p-aminodiethylaniline sulfate", i.e. para-amino with an N,N-
#:             diethyl substitution.
_DEVELOPMENT_PROGRESS: dict[str, DevelopmentProgress] = {
    # metol-hydroquinone == D72's agent pair
    "EASTMAN_DOUBLE_X_5222": DevelopmentProgress.GRANULAR,   # KODAK D-96
    "ILFORD_FP4":            DevelopmentProgress.GRANULAR,   # ID-11
    "ILFORD_HP3":            DevelopmentProgress.GRANULAR,   # ID-11
    "ILFORD_HPS":            DevelopmentProgress.GRANULAR,   # ID-11
    "ILFORD_PAN_F":          DevelopmentProgress.GRANULAR,   # ID-11
    "KENTMERE_PAN_100":      DevelopmentProgress.GRANULAR,   # ID-11
    "KENTMERE_PAN_400":      DevelopmentProgress.GRANULAR,   # ID-11
    # 4-amino-N-dialkylaniline == CP-20's agent class
    "SVEMA_DS_4":            DevelopmentProgress.PARALLEL,   # ЦПВ-1
    "SVEMA_DS_5M":           DevelopmentProgress.PARALLEL,   # ЦПВ-1
}

#: ⚠ CONFIRMED FROM A SECOND, INDEPENDENT DIRECTION 2026-08-27 (task A2).
#: Figs. 7.10/7.11 sweep SULFUR SENSITIZATION on the same emulsion at the same
#: 0.1 s exposure, changing only the developer, and reach the same A/B split
#: through development RATE rather than through grain-state fractions:
#:     CP-20 (parallel)  rate 0.769 / 0.779 / 0.788 / 0.740 min^-1
#:                       -> FLAT to +-3 % across the whole sweep
#:     D72   (granular)  rate 2.681 -> 1.074 -> 0.794 -> 0.639 min^-1
#:                       -> falls by a factor of 4.2
#: Mechanism: granular development is rate-limited by the FIRST ELECTRON
#: INJECTION into a development centre, so dispersing the centres (more sulfur,
#: or a higher light intensity) slows it; parallel development is limited by
#: the grain's own surface-to-volume ratio, which sensitization does not touch.
#: The same split Fig. 7.12 shows from the other side (parallel rate ~ 1/d,
#: granular rate independent of d). Full traced tables: knowledge base §23b.
#: NO CONSTANT CHANGED as a result -- this is corroboration, not new data.
#:
#: Traced constants that go with each progress type. Both come off Tani's
#: figures, measured on sulfur-sensitized cubic AgBr of 0.86 um at 0.1 s:
#:   partial_fill_fraction  the mean fraction of grains caught mid-development.
#:                          CP-20 ~0.45 (a large developing band at every
#:                          stage), D72 ~0.04 (a thin sliver)
#:                          [Tani Figs. 7.8/7.9, pp.215-216 / PDF 224-225].
#:   rate_size_coeff        r = coeff / d for PARALLEL development, 0.591
#:                          um/min by through-origin least squares on the three
#:                          octahedral-AgBr points of Tani Fig. 7.12 (p.219 /
#:                          PDF 227); the book's own drawn line is ~0.64.
#:                          ⚠ OMITTED for GRANULAR, where the companion text
#:                          states the rate is nearly INDEPENDENT of grain
#:                          size -- a 1/d coefficient there would assert the
#:                          opposite of the source, and ProcessingSpec.validate
#:                          rejects it.
_PROGRESS_CONSTANTS = {
    DevelopmentProgress.PARALLEL: (0.45, 0.591),
    DevelopmentProgress.GRANULAR: (0.04, 0.0),
}


