            source="⚠ SECOND EDITION OF THE SAME PUBLICATION, SUPPLIED BY THE OWNER 2026-08-26 AND IT IS THE ONE THAT CAN BE READ: Eastman Kodak Company, «EASTMAN DOUBLE-X Negative Film 5222/7222 -- Technical Data», KODAK Publication No. H-1-5222, Revised 7-15 (header JULY 2015), (c) Eastman Kodak Company 2015 -- PDF/PROFILES/KODAK/EASTMAN DOUBLE-X Negative Film 5222.pdf, 3 pages, text layer present. THE DECISIVE DIFFERENCE IS NOT THE CONTENT BUT THE ART: this edition draws EVERY PLOT AS VECTOR PATHS and embeds no images at all, where the revised 3-26 edition already on file prints the identical figures as RASTERS (its p3 carries three images against three drawing paths). Same figure numbers, F010_0029AC for the sensitometric panel and F010_0031AC for the spectral one, so these are two printings of one plot set eleven years apart and not two measurements. HARVESTED FROM IT 2026-08-26, four adoptions and one correction: (1) MTF MEASURED for the first time -- p2 vector Modulation-Transfer panel, tungsten, D-96 to control gamma, diffuse visual -- f50 42.2 cycles/mm with rolloff q 2.88 and a printed +25 % adjacency overshoot peaking at 4.1 cycles/mm, replacing the flat estimate 56.0/56.0/56.0 which was 1.33x too sharp; CROSS-CHECKED against the sister stock PLUS-X 5231, the corpus's other Kodak black-and-white cine negative, which measures 41.3 off its own sheet. (2) SPECTRAL SENSITIVITY re-traced from the p3 vector paths and the DENSITY CRITERION READ FROM THE PANEL'S OWN CAPTION: the sheet draws TWO curves, 'D = 0.3 Above Gross Fog' and 'D = 1.0 Above Gross Fog', and the adopted set is the D 1.0 one, chosen by matching that caption to the curve beneath it. It agrees with the 2026-08-02 raster reading of the same figure to rms 0.037 decades on the same 430 nm peak. (3) PROCESSING FAMILY populated from the five printed per-curve gamma labels -- 4 min 0.50, 5 min 0.56, 6 1/2 min 0.66, 9 min 0.84, 12 min 1.05 in D-96 at 21 C. (4) BASE+FOG CORRECTED 0.1977 -> 0.2328: the 2026-08-02 raster trace of this same curve got the SHAPE right (its gamma is within 0.0004 of the vector refit, and it reproduces the vector path to rms 0.0123 D) and the LEVEL wrong by 0.035 D. Confirmed two independent ways before changing it -- calibrating the density axis from the five printed ticks gives 0.2369, calibrating it from the frame edges gives 0.2281, and 0.1977 sits outside both. (5) DEVELOPER CORRECTED, and this is the substantive one: _PROCESSING said 'Kodak D-76' from Iofis 1964, while Kodak's own sheet says D-96 at 21 C in three separate places -- the PROCESSING table, the sensitometric panel caption and the MTF panel caption. D-76 is a still-film developer. The Iofis row is kept for what it does evidence (local 1963-64 practice, plus its independent confirmation of the ASA 250/200 pair and the 0,6-0,7 gamma band) rather than deleted. ⚠ STILL NOT PRINTED ON EITHER EDITION: any sigma(D) granularity SHAPE (the sheet gives the single rms 14 and points at KODAK Publication H-845 for image structure, which this corpus does not hold), a numeric Dmax, and any reciprocity exponent beyond the 1/10,000 s to 1 s no-correction statement. ",
